{
  "courseSlug": "understanding-startup-equity-valuation-and-cap-tables-for-investors",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "title": "Chapter 5: From Paper Valuation to Real Money",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "title": "Case Study: Following One ₹5 Lakh Angel Cheque Through Four Rounds to Exit",
          "slug": "case-study-following-one-5-lakh-angel-cheque-through-four-rounds-to-exit",
          "body": [
            {
              "_key": "k1",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Every idea in this course has had its own lesson. Real startups do not arrive one idea at a time. A single angel cheque goes through a convertible, an ESOP pool, a round, a down round, anti-dilution, a pro-rata decision, a recovery, a preference stack and finally an exit, and every one of those events changes what the cheque is worth. This capstone follows one fictional investor, Ritu, and her ₹5 lakh from the day she signs an iSAFE to the day cash lands in her account, using the tools you have built across the course.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "bigIdea",
              "text": "Your stake is shaped by every event on the cap table, not just the headline valuation. Track the shares, the price and what sits ahead of you at each step, and the final payout stops being a surprise.",
              "_key": "k3"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k4",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k5",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The Journey at a Glance",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "timeline",
              "title": "Ritu's ₹5 lakh in DhobiGo (illustrative)",
              "events": [
                {
                  "_key": "k7",
                  "date": "2021",
                  "title": "Pre-seed iSAFE",
                  "description": "Ritu, a Bhubaneswar product designer, puts ₹5 lakh into DhobiGo Laundry Technologies, a fictional app-based laundry pickup startup, via an iSAFE alongside other angels."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k9",
                  "date": "2022",
                  "title": "Seed round",
                  "description": "A seed fund invests. An ESOP pool is created and the iSAFEs convert."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k11",
                  "date": "2023",
                  "title": "Series A",
                  "description": "A Series A fund invests at a higher price, with a pool top-up. Ritu declines her pro-rata."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k13",
                  "date": "2024",
                  "title": "Series B down round",
                  "description": "Funding winter. The company raises at a lower price, and Series A anti-dilution kicks in."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k15",
                  "date": "2025",
                  "title": "Series C",
                  "description": "Growth returns and a Series C is priced well above every previous round."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k17",
                  "date": "2027",
                  "title": "Exit",
                  "description": "A listed consumer services company acquires DhobiGo for cash."
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k18"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k19",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k20",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Stage 1: The iSAFE and the Seed Round",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k21",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k22",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Founders Aarav and Leena hold 10,00,000 shares. Angels, including Ritu, invest ₹75 lakh through iSAFEs with a ₹6 crore valuation cap and a 20% discount. A year later, a seed fund invests ₹4.5 crore at a ₹17.25 crore pre-money valuation, which includes a new ESOP pool of 1,50,000 options.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "Seed round mechanics",
              "headers": [
                "Item",
                "Calculation",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k24",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Seed price per share",
                    "₹17.25 crore ÷ (10,00,000 + 1,50,000 pool)",
                    "₹150"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k26",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "iSAFE discount price",
                    "₹150 × 0.8",
                    "₹120"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k28",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "iSAFE cap price",
                    "₹6 crore ÷ 10,00,000",
                    "₹60"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k30",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Conversion price used",
                    "Lower of ₹120 and ₹60",
                    "₹60 (cap wins)"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k32",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Ritu's shares",
                    "₹5 lakh ÷ ₹60, rounded down",
                    "8,333"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k34",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "All angels' shares",
                    "₹75 lakh ÷ ₹60",
                    "1,25,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k36",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Seed fund shares",
                    "₹4.5 crore ÷ ₹150",
                    "3,00,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k38",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Total shares after seed",
                    "10,00,000 + 1,50,000 + 1,25,000 + 3,00,000",
                    "15,75,000"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k39"
            },
            {
              "_type": "statGrid",
              "stats": [
                {
                  "_key": "k41",
                  "label": "Ritu's stake",
                  "value": "0.529%",
                  "context": "8,333 ÷ 15,75,000"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k43",
                  "label": "Paper value",
                  "value": "₹12.5 lakh",
                  "context": "8,333 × ₹150"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k45",
                  "label": "Paper multiple",
                  "value": "2.5x",
                  "context": "The cap did the work"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k46"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "The valuation cap was Ritu's reward for investing first. The seed fund paid ₹150 per share, while Ritu's money converted at ₹60. Without a cap, she would have converted at the ₹120 discount price and received only 4,166 shares, half as many.",
              "_key": "k47"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k48",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k49",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Stage 2: Series A and the Pro-Rata Decision",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k50",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k51",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The Series A fund invests ₹15 crore at a ₹66 crore pre-money valuation, which includes a 75,000-option pool top-up. The price is ₹66 crore ÷ (15,75,000 + 75,000) = ₹400 per share, and the fund receives 3,75,000 Series A CCPS with 1x non-participating preference and broad-based weighted average anti-dilution. Total shares rise to 20,25,000.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "statGrid",
              "stats": [
                {
                  "_key": "k53",
                  "label": "Ritu's stake",
                  "value": "0.412%",
                  "context": "8,333 ÷ 20,25,000"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k55",
                  "label": "Paper value",
                  "value": "₹33.3 lakh",
                  "context": "8,333 × ₹400"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k57",
                  "label": "Her pro-rata allocation",
                  "value": "₹7.94 lakh",
                  "context": "0.529% × ₹15 crore"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k58"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k59",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k60",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Ritu's startup budget is ₹50 lakh across ten companies. Putting another ₹7.94 lakh into DhobiGo would make it more than a quarter of her portfolio, so she declines. It is a reasonable portfolio decision, and the rest of the story shows what it cost and saved her.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k61",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k62",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Stage 3: The Series B Down Round",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k63",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k64",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "In the 2024 funding winter, growth slows and DhobiGo raises ₹12 crore at ₹250 per share, below the ₹400 Series A price. The Series B investor receives 4,80,000 CCPS. The Series A fund's broad-based weighted average protection now triggers.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "CP_2 = ₹400 \\times \\frac{20{,}25{,}000 + 3{,}00{,}000}{20{,}25{,}000 + 4{,}80{,}000} = ₹371.26",
              "caption": "B = ₹12 crore ÷ ₹400 = 3,00,000; C = 4,80,000",
              "_key": "k65"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k66",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k67",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Series A shares on conversion: ₹15 crore ÷ ₹371.26 = 4,04,032, which is 29,032 extra shares.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k68",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k69",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Ritu's iSAFE converted at ₹60, and the seed fund paid ₹150. Both are below ₹250, so neither gets any adjustment.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k70",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k71",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Total shares: 20,25,000 + 4,80,000 + 29,032 = 25,34,032.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_type": "statGrid",
              "stats": [
                {
                  "_key": "k73",
                  "label": "Ritu's stake",
                  "value": "0.329%",
                  "context": "8,333 ÷ 25,34,032"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k75",
                  "label": "Paper value",
                  "value": "₹20.8 lakh",
                  "context": "8,333 × ₹250, down from ₹33.3 lakh"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k77",
                  "label": "Still above cost",
                  "value": "4.2x",
                  "context": "Her low entry price protects her"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k78"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "warning",
              "text": "If Ritu had taken her ₹7.94 lakh Series A pro-rata at ₹400, that money would have been worth only ₹4.96 lakh on paper after the down round. Declining looked sensible at this stage. Pro-rata decisions can only be judged against what happens next, which is why position sizing matters more than prediction.",
              "_key": "k79"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k80",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k81",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Stage 4: Series C Recovery",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k82",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k83",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Growth returns. A Series C fund invests ₹40 crore at ₹800 per share, a pre-money valuation of about ₹202.72 crore, for 5,00,000 CCPS. Total shares reach 30,34,032, and the post-money valuation is about ₹242.72 crore.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
