                {
                  "_key": "k107",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Her ownership roughly halved from 0.529% to 0.275%, while her paper value rose more than thirteenfold. That is compounding dilution working in her favour, because the price per share rose far faster than her percentage fell.",
                  "marks": []
