            },
            {
              "_key": "k111",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k112",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "In 2027, a listed consumer services company buys DhobiGo for ₹300 crore in cash. Venture debt and transaction costs take ₹10 crore, leaving ₹290 crore for shareholders. Every CCPS series has a 1x non-participating preference, with later series senior, adding up to a ₹72.25 crore preference stack.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k113",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k114",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Run the waterfall. If everyone converts, each share receives ₹290 crore ÷ 30,34,032 = ₹955.82. That is higher than the price paid by every series, including Series C at ₹800, so every investor converts and the proceeds are shared purely by ownership.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
